```
if (i===0){x=5;z=7;} else if(i===1){x=-7;z=5;}
...
if (Math.hypot(x-player.pos.x,z-player.pos.z)<6.5) { x += ... }
```
But if random close, shift. Use `if(distance<7){ const a=Math.atan2(x-player.pos.x,z-player.pos.z); x=player.pos.x+Math.sin(a)*7; z=player.pos.z+Math.cos(a)*7; }` to push outward. That keeps distribution. Good.
- The NPCs in the screenshot are missing shadows? They have some shadows on ground. Good.
- The gun is still a giant black block at bottom right. It looks like a big rectangular slab. The model isn't reading as a rifle because the camera is close and we see the side of the body/stock. We should improve the gun model or reduce it further. It occupies ~20% width and 30% height. Typical FPS. But the shape is just a black rectangle with a smaller black rectangle below. It doesn't look like a rifle. We can add details: a brown stock, a scope, a barrel that extends forward, a magazine, maybe make it smaller. The current rifle model has body .18x.16x.52, stock .16x.18x.24 at z .32, barrel .09x.08x.3 at z -.31, grip .12x.24x.14. In the screenshot, we see a big black rectangular block (stock?) and a smaller block below (grip), and maybe barrel hidden. The perspective is from the side/back; the barrel extends forward but may be hidden behind the body due camera. We can rotate the gun slightly to show the barrel: `gun.rotation.y = -.12` maybe. And add a brown stock to contrast. Also move it slightly left? The gun at x .4, y -.34, z -1.02. The body is at the right. Maybe use x .3 and z -1.15, scale .8. 
- Add color: stock `wood`, body `dark`, barrel `steel`, magazine `black`. The screenshot shows all black because `cachedMat('#303a36')` is dark green/black, and `materials.black` is near black. The stock is black? In buildGun for rifle:
```
cube(gun, 0,0,0,.18,.16,.52,dark);
